Synthesis
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The D/U/N ledger is a labelled hitting-set hypergraph.
Open-gap lifts are not failures of the ledger; they are full covers whose
exact pair-sum witness rises above the floor but stays below the unit-shell edge.
Private obligations identify descent pivots: replacing or lowering a runner must
preserve its private D/U/N labels or immediately creates a clock witness.
This is the owner-labelled event word requested by the Burnside/Fourier framing,
but compressed to the obligations that are provably necessary for sub-edge rows.
